    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nO'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers are delighted to offer an elegant 1940s Residence on circa 1-Acre Elevated Site in Beaghbeg, Caherlistrane, Co. Galway\n\nThe property not only contains a stunning residential building but also a range of substantial structures. \n\nThe corner store, now unused but once a prime commercial enterprise in Caherlistrane. Numerous outhouses with existing stabling suitable for a variety of uses.\n\nConstructed in the mid-1940s, this charming home has been primely located in Caherlistrane for its entirety. This light-filled, architect-designed detached home is set on a beautifully landscaped one-acre elevated site in Beaghbeg, Caherlistrane. \n\nA stones throw from the local National School and only 180 metres from the Roman Catholic Church, the location offers a peaceful, community-focused lifestyle in the heart of north Galway.\n\nThe property has stunning original features and could benefit from modernisation to suit a purchasers style. The property could be a candidate for government refurbishment grants. \n\nThe manicured gardens are filled with mature shrubs and colourful blooms year-round, offering a picturesque setting with dual gated access.\n\nThe dwelling house extends to approx. 150 sq. metres and comprises 4 to 5 bedrooms, a living room, sitting room, kitchen, two bathrooms, and a utility room generously proportioned throughout.\n\nThe large attic also provides excellent additional space. A key feature Is the light that shines through each room.\n\nThis sale presents an abundance of potential. Rarely does a substantial site in a prime location come to the market with a fabulous dwelling house, mature gardens with additional outbuildings suitable for repurpose STPP. \n\nLocated 26 km from Galway City, and within a 4550 minute drive of both Westport and Castlebar, it's also just minutes from nearby towns: Headford (8 km) and Shrule (5 km).\n\nKeep up to-date with NEW PROPERTIES by registering your details on our database \n\nFor Further details please contact our office on 091-564212 \nOFFICE OPENING HOURS - MON TO FRI 9AM TO 5:30PM\n\nProperties can be viewed on our website www.odj.ie \n\nNOTE: These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer. They are for information only and give a general idea of the property. They are not to be taken as forming any part of a resulting contract, nor to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. Whilst every care is taken in their preparation, neither O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers nor the vendor accept any liability as to their accuracy. Intending purchasers must satisfy themselves by personal inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of these particulars. No person in the employment of O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Built c. 1940</li><li> Architect-designed layout with excellent natural light</li><li> Beautiful, mature gardens with colourful year-round planting.</li><li> Substantial outhouses with stabling — development potential (STPP)</li><li> Dual gated access, private driveway & ample parking</li><li> Oil-fired central heating (OFCH)</li><li> Private septic tank & public water supply</li><li> Located in a scenic, peaceful area, close to school, church & GAA club</li><li> Spacious attic offering further storage or potential</ul>"
      },
